  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on qualitative data from a small sample of 21 experts in two frontrunner cities, which may limit their direct applicability to cities with less municipal capacity or different regulatory contexts.",
      "what": "This study identifies the key actors, barriers, and solutions for integrating nature-based solutions (NBS) into urban business ecosystems by analyzing two Finnish cities participating in the EU Mission on Climate-Neutral and Smart Cities. Based on interviews and focus groups with 21 experts in 2023, the research outlines seven thematic solution areas for scaling NBS, including economic instruments, policy tools, and collaborative business models.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that the success of urban nature-based solutions depends on a highly active city-business interface, positioning municipal governments as multi-role facilitators rather than just regulators in local green business ecosystems."
    }
  },
